# C – CONTEXT

**Project Name:** ReVive AI

**Project Category:** Artificial Intelligence, E-Waste Management, Computer Vision, Drone Technology, GPS Tracking and Sustainable Recycling.

## 1. Problem Statement

Electronic waste is increasing rapidly due to the frequent replacement of electronic gadgets and devices.

Many people have unused, unwanted or damaged electronic gadgets stored in their homes, offices and institutions. Other electronic waste is discarded in unauthorized locations, streets and open dumping areas.

The major challenges include:

- People do not know where or how to dispose of unused electronic gadgets.
- Electronic waste is often mixed with ordinary garbage.
- Illegal e-waste dumping locations are difficult to identify and monitor.
- Waste collection teams lack centralized location information.
- Collection activities are difficult to track in real time.
- Recycling organizations may not have accurate information about collected materials.
- Valuable reusable electronic components are often wasted instead of being recovered.

## 2. Proposed Solution

ReVive AI is an intelligent e-waste detection, reporting, location tracking and collection management platform.

The system enables citizens, organizations and institutions to report unused or unwanted electronic gadgets through image uploads.

AI analyzes uploaded images and identifies the type of electronic waste.

Drones capture aerial images of dumping areas and help detect, map and monitor e-waste accumulation locations.

GPS technology records reported waste locations and tracks authorized collection workers during assigned collection activities.

Administrators monitor waste reports, drone captures, collection orders, workers, inspections and recovery operations through a centralized dashboard.

The physical waste is collected by human collection teams, transported to designated facilities, inspected and directed towards reuse, refurbishment, recycling or safe disposal.

**Core Vision: Turn unused electronics and improperly discarded e-waste into tracked, recoverable resources.**

